  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this dashboard is",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Iris's turns, from the thalamus's own OTLP spans** (row thalamus-otel-panel; spans: src/otel.rs). On only while `thalamus_otel_spans: true`; off, every table here is empty, and that means *off*, not *quiet*.\n\nA turn is `iris.turn`; under it, one `iris.complete` per model request and one `iris.tool` per tool call. Spans carry names, durations, the model id, a tool's name, the outcome and token counts, never what the person typed or a row value: the thalamus ledger stays the place for content, and a trace id here is the ledger's session uuid without dashes.\n\nThese are TraceQL **searches**, not rates: this Tempo runs no metrics generator, so a rate panel would draw nothing and look calm."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Turns: the latest, slowest first in the duration column",
      "description": "One row per Iris turn with its duration and the turn's token counts.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "tempo",
        "uid": "tempo"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "tempo",
            "uid": "tempo"
          },
          "queryType": "traceql",
          "query": "{resource.service.name=\"thalamus\" && name=\"iris.turn\"} | select(span.gen_ai.usage.input_tokens, span.gen_ai.usage.output_tokens)",
          "limit": 50,
          "tableType": "traces"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Errors and refusals: any span that ended in error",
      "description": "A model request or tool call that failed, or a turn whose children failed. The ledger says why.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "tempo",
        "uid": "tempo"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
